{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשמר", :translit "l'shamer", :gloss "to guard"} {:he "לילין שדין מזיקין רוחין", :translit "lilin shedin mazikin ruchin", :gloss "night-demons, field-demons, harming-spirits, winds"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "לשמר", :expansion ["לילין" "שדין" "מזיקין" "רוחין"]}], :frame {:text "The verse states that God stationed cherubim and the flame of the turning sword 'to guard (l'shamer)' the way to the Tree of Life (Genesis 3:24). The verb לשמר, 'to guard,' is understood to specify what is being guarded against: destructive beings such as demons and harmful spirits. Rabbinic literature assumes the existence of various classes of demons and spirits that populate the world, including night-demons, field-demons, and harmful winds (Berakhot 6a; Pesachim 112b–113a).", :sources ["Genesis 3:24" "Berakhot 6a" "Pesachim 112b" "Pesachim 113a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "לשמר", :expansion ["לילין" "שדין" "מזיקין" "רוחין"], :initials ["ל" "ש" "מ" "ר"], :by :selah, :initials-match? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:24.489086817Z", :model "glm-5.2"}